UPSTREAM DATA PROVIDER ATTRIBUTION & TERMS NOTICE
-------------------------------------------------
OmniEarth is an open-source orchestration and aggregation engine. It does not
own, host, or re-license any upstream satellite imagery, meteorological feeds,
soil models, or environmental datasets accessed through its adapters.

Users and downstream applications remain solely responsible for complying with
each upstream data provider's sovereign license and data usage terms, including:
- ESA / Copernicus Open Access Policy (Sentinel-1, Sentinel-2, Sentinel-3,
  Sentinel-5P, Sentinel-6, Copernicus DEM, ESA WorldCover)
- USGS / NASA Open Data Policy (Landsat 8/9, NASA EMIT, NASA FIRMS,
  NASA GPM IMERG, NASA SMAP, Suomi-NPP / NOAA VIIRS)
- German Aerospace Center (DLR) EnMAP Data Policy and User License
- Open-Meteo & ECMWF Public Terms (CC BY 4.0)
- ISRIC SoilGrids Open Data License (CC BY 4.0)
- JAXA ALOS AW3D30 Open Data Policy & OpenTopography S3 Archive
